\ Exp 032: Flow control macros — composable from Forth

\ BOOL` — convert FLAGS-based condition to boolean (-1/0) on stack
\ Pushes 0, then if condition true, NOTs to -1.
: BOOL` 0 lit` IF` ~` THEN` ;

\ SKIP` — unconditional forward jump (long, E9 rel32)
\ Pushes patch address for THEN` to resolve.
: SKIP` >S0 $E9, ,1 here 4 allot ;

\ ELSE` — IF-true path ends with JMP, then patch IF's forward ref
: ELSE` SKIP` swap THEN` ;

\ CASE` — test equality, enter body if match, else continue
\ Usage: val  1 CASE body1  ELSE  2 CASE body2  ELSE  default drop  THEN THEN
: CASE` =` drop` IF` drop` ;

\ Test helper: macro that always pushes 65 (skipping 42 via SKIP`)
: skiptest` SKIP` 42 lit` THEN` 65 lit` ;

\ Test helper: macro using IF`/ELSE`/THEN` composition
: ifelsetest` 0-` 0=` IF` 65 lit` ELSE` 66 lit` THEN` ;
